WEBVTT

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.575
[PHOENIX] I'm Phoenix Wright,
attorney-at-law,

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:05.742
and my next case takes
place in a peculiar venue.

00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:08.950
A luxury express train, shooting
northward through the snow--

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.492
The Silver Star.

00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:14.200
Inside its exquisite dining car,
a trial is about to begin.

00:00:14.283 --> 00:00:17.200
It's a bizarre setting, but
my extremely unusual client

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.575
fits right in.

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:24.117
If you'd come to order,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.200
court is now in session
for the trial of fugitive

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:28.825
Avery Richman!

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.033
[PHOENIX] December 31:
Maya and I have been invited

00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:08.283
to ring in the New Year
with a luxurious trip

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:11.658
on the maiden voyage of
a one of a kind railway liner.

00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:14.200
Now. The moment you've
been waiting for.

00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.783
We're proud to bring you the
ultimate in first-class travel.

00:02:16.867 --> 00:02:19.825
Ladies and gentlemen--
The Silver Star Express!

00:02:19.908 --> 00:02:21.867
This train is a
labor of love, folks.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.242
Love for the elegance of the
steam-powered locomotive,

00:02:24.325 --> 00:02:25.700
and Japan itself.

00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.117
A gift to our society from
the Goldstruck Republic's

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.992
prominent tycoon, Avery Richman!

00:02:32.075 --> 00:02:33.992
Mr. Richman sends his blessings.

00:02:34.075 --> 00:02:37.408
Sadly, he couldn't be here to
celebrate this occasion with us,

00:02:37.492 --> 00:02:41.242
but regardless, we'll be
departing soon, so all aboard!

00:02:41.325 --> 00:02:45.242
This is so cool!
A luxury choo-choo train!

00:02:45.325 --> 00:02:47.325
I think it's all
very nostal-chic.

00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:49.200
I think you mean nostal-gic.

00:02:52.783 --> 00:02:56.117
Ooh! Come on!
Let's climb on board, Nick!

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.783
[GUMSHOE]
Whoa, you two again?

00:02:57.867 --> 00:02:58.867
[MAYA gasps]

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.283
[PHOENIX]
Hello, Detective Gumshoe.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.033
[MAYA]
Hello, Judge. Judge?

00:03:02.117 --> 00:03:04.033
Hello. Nice day.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.658
We both sent in
a postcard and won a trip!

00:03:06.742 --> 00:03:08.492
I'm going on an
all-expenses paid tour of

00:03:08.575 --> 00:03:11.533
the hot springs up north on
board this old-timey train!

00:03:11.617 --> 00:03:14.325
Yeah? We got an invitation!

00:03:14.408 --> 00:03:16.117
With a fancy wax seal!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.367
Wha--? Personally invited?

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.950
So which car are you two in?

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.700
We'll be right up front
in the first one.

00:03:21.783 --> 00:03:23.658
They put us back in car 3.

00:03:23.742 --> 00:03:25.617
We should totally meet up later!

00:03:28.492 --> 00:03:29.617
Here.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.992
Thank you very much, young lady.

00:03:32.075 --> 00:03:33.742
Miss Maya Fey and
Mister Phoenix Wright,

00:03:33.825 --> 00:03:35.992
welcome to the Silver Star.

00:03:36.075 --> 00:03:37.617
It's a pleasure
to meet you both.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.700
My name is Rick and I'll be
your attendant on this journey.

00:03:40.783 --> 00:03:42.242
[MAYA]
Pleasure to meet you, too!

00:03:42.325 --> 00:03:44.742
I see you'll be staying
in the Sakura Room today.

00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:46.200
The Sakura Room?

00:03:46.283 --> 00:03:49.617
Ah! Even the name screams
"traditional elegance!"

00:03:50.992 --> 00:03:52.950
I can't wait to see inside!

00:03:54.658 --> 00:03:58.658
[MAYA giggles]
It's absolutely beautiful!

00:03:58.742 --> 00:04:00.492
Wow, we get our own compartment.

00:04:00.575 --> 00:04:04.700
[MAYA giggles]
This is great! Travel in style!

00:04:04.783 --> 00:04:06.783
[PHOENIX sighs]
Very nice.

00:04:06.867 --> 00:04:08.450
I'm so happy you like it!

00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:11.075
Mister Richman had the idea
for a private rail line.

00:04:11.158 --> 00:04:14.450
So he bought an unused one
and gave us the Silver Star.

00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:16.575
We take great
pride in the design.

00:04:16.658 --> 00:04:19.325
Its retro look is inspired by
the old steam engine trains

00:04:19.408 --> 00:04:20.867
from the 1950s.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.200
[GUMSHOE gasps]

00:04:22.283 --> 00:04:24.242
[RICK] No detail inside or
out has been overlooked.

00:04:24.325 --> 00:04:26.825
Although the styling harkens
back to an earlier time,

00:04:26.908 --> 00:04:28.742
the train's engines
and propulsion system

00:04:28.825 --> 00:04:30.742
are cutting edge technologies.

00:04:31.742 --> 00:04:34.033
By the way.
In case you're interested.

00:04:34.117 --> 00:04:35.992
Every single crew member
aboard hails from

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.367
Mister Richman's homeland.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.992
[MAYA]
Oh, that means you, too?

00:04:39.075 --> 00:04:42.200
Yes. I'm originally from
the Goldstruck Republic.

00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:45.117
I hear Mister Richman's really
into Japanese culture.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.658
And he even recently became
a naturalized citizen.

00:04:47.742 --> 00:04:48.908
[RICK]
That's true.

00:04:48.992 --> 00:04:51.158
Ah. That explains
why there's a Sakura Room.

00:04:51.242 --> 00:04:53.117
This railway is
a coming together of a lot

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.033
of Mister Richman's interests.

00:04:55.117 --> 00:04:56.492
His dreams.

00:04:56.575 --> 00:04:58.617
We hope your journey
is a pleasant one.

00:05:00.075 --> 00:05:02.617
Wow, this is really
something else.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.158
Makes ya wonder why someone
like you got an invitation.

00:05:05.242 --> 00:05:06.783
I mean, I never had
a clue that you were

00:05:06.867 --> 00:05:08.533
such a big shot, Nick.

00:05:08.617 --> 00:05:10.575
Yeah, it's kinda funny
you mention that.

00:05:10.658 --> 00:05:13.242
I don't have any sort of
connection to Mr. Richman.

00:05:13.325 --> 00:05:16.242
So I'm actually at a loss
as to why I was invited.

00:05:16.325 --> 00:05:19.575
I guess it is a mystery
why he'd ask some nobody.

00:05:19.658 --> 00:05:20.700
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:22.450
Anyway, let's look around.

00:05:22.533 --> 00:05:23.992
Explore a bit!

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.908
Hurry up!

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:27.908
[PHOENIX sighs]

00:05:27.992 --> 00:05:29.242
Of course, sir.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.908
Pardon me. Where is
the Chrysanthemum Room?

00:05:36.992 --> 00:05:38.283
[RICK]
Follow me, sir.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.950
Long time no see.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.575
Yes, indeed.

00:05:43.658 --> 00:05:44.700
[RICK]
Having a look around?

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.117
You know it!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.533
[RICK]
Nice! Have fun!

00:05:49.325 --> 00:05:50.533
Here we are, sir.

00:05:50.617 --> 00:05:51.992
I appreciate it.

00:05:55.575 --> 00:05:56.867
[BOTH gasp]

00:05:59.075 --> 00:06:01.408
[police sirens blaring]

00:06:01.492 --> 00:06:02.950
[VOICE A]
Attention, all units!

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:06.242
The fugitive has escaped the
flight and is still at large.

00:06:06.325 --> 00:06:08.492
Set up checkpoints
on every transportation system

00:06:08.575 --> 00:06:09.533
in the area.

00:06:09.617 --> 00:06:11.158
If you do encounter
the fugitive,

00:06:11.242 --> 00:06:14.033
please exercise extreme
caution when approaching.

00:06:14.117 --> 00:06:17.075
We cannot risk the
safety of civilians.

00:06:17.158 --> 00:06:18.533
[COP A] Looks like
there's a nasty storm

00:06:18.617 --> 00:06:19.908
coming our way tonight.

00:06:19.992 --> 00:06:21.700
[COP B] Yeah, that's not
gonna make this any easier.

00:06:21.783 --> 00:06:23.575
We've definitely got
our work cut out for us.

00:06:23.658 --> 00:06:26.283
[COP A] Last thing we need
is a diplomatic crisis.

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:28.617
[MAYA] Hey, we're right
next to the dining car!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.450
That's pretty convenient!

00:06:31.533 --> 00:06:32.992
[BOTH gasp]

00:06:33.075 --> 00:06:35.950
[PHOENIX] Wonder if the
food's as rich as the décor.

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.575
[REGINA]
I didn't know. We can't do it.

00:06:38.658 --> 00:06:39.992
[ATTENDANT A] But we
have specific orders from

00:06:40.075 --> 00:06:41.367
Mister Richman that
we're to meet all

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.283
the passengers' demands.
No matter what they may be.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:46.033
The king said that?

00:06:46.117 --> 00:06:48.075
[sighs]

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:51.325
Well, if that's the case,
please come this way.

00:06:51.408 --> 00:06:52.325
Thanks.

00:06:52.408 --> 00:06:54.242
Some kind of trouble. I guess?

00:06:54.325 --> 00:06:55.408
[bell rings]

00:06:55.492 --> 00:06:56.742
[MAYA gasps]

00:06:57.658 --> 00:06:59.742
[CONDUCTOR A]
All aboard!

00:06:59.825 --> 00:07:01.783
[whistle blows]

00:07:21.492 --> 00:07:24.825
[MAYA] Man, that was
a beautiful sunset.

00:07:24.908 --> 00:07:26.075
Don't you think so, Nick?

00:07:26.158 --> 00:07:28.117
[gasps, growls]

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.617
[PHOENIX]
After receiving the invitation,

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.992
I did a little digging
into Mister Avery Richman.

00:07:33.075 --> 00:07:34.575
Not like I hadn't heard of him.

00:07:34.658 --> 00:07:36.367
He's one of the
world's wealthiest men,

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.283
and he'd made the news when
he became a Japanese citizen

00:07:39.367 --> 00:07:41.908
and purchased an
entire railroad line.

00:07:41.992 --> 00:07:45.408
[gasps]
What's that?

00:07:45.492 --> 00:07:47.325
Ahoy, Steel Samurai.

00:07:47.408 --> 00:07:49.075
Come again?

00:07:49.158 --> 00:07:50.450
Pretty cool, huh?

00:07:50.533 --> 00:07:53.533
But what's even cooler
is that it's a transceiver!

00:07:53.617 --> 00:07:55.992
Yeah, but what are
we gonna do with transceivers?

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.575
[MAYA]
Isn't that obvious?

00:07:57.658 --> 00:07:59.492
We're gonna play bomb squad.

00:07:59.575 --> 00:08:01.450
Oh. You don't say?

00:08:01.533 --> 00:08:05.117
Come in, Vanguard, tell me
you've found the bomb. Over.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.450
[MAYA] Yes, sir! It has
a red wire and a blue one.

00:08:07.533 --> 00:08:10.075
What do we do? Please! Help!

00:08:10.158 --> 00:08:12.992
Ugh! To hell with being careful!

00:08:13.075 --> 00:08:15.033
Cut all of 'em, now!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.408
You're nuts.

00:08:19.492 --> 00:08:20.783
I just think we can
have fun with games about

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:22.908
runaway trains and bomb scares!

00:08:22.992 --> 00:08:24.825
You've been watching
way too many movies.

00:08:24.908 --> 00:08:26.700
[knocking]

00:08:26.783 --> 00:08:28.492
I came to hang out with my pals!

00:08:28.575 --> 00:08:30.408
[MAYA]
Hey there, Gummy!

00:08:30.492 --> 00:08:32.283
[GUMSHOE] Thanks for showing
me the way, Regina.

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.992
Much appreciated!

00:08:34.075 --> 00:08:36.825
I'm glad to help!
You guys have fun, okay?

00:08:42.283 --> 00:08:45.367
Commence with the operation.
We'll secure our king.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.158
Right. There was an issue
in the dining car earlier.

00:08:48.242 --> 00:08:49.617
Yes, I heard.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.908
Special request from
a valued passenger.

00:08:51.992 --> 00:08:54.783
It's unexpected, but we
still have to fulfill it.

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.783
--Right.
--Nothing to worry about.

00:08:56.867 --> 00:08:58.783
Stick to the plan
and it'll be fine.

00:08:58.867 --> 00:09:00.825
[REGINA]
Yeah.

00:09:00.908 --> 00:09:02.242
[sighs]

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.033
[door clacks]

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.742
[RICK]
May I help you with something?

00:09:08.825 --> 00:09:10.492
Some scotch. Neat.

00:09:10.575 --> 00:09:12.992
I'll get right
on it, sir. No problem.

00:09:17.783 --> 00:09:19.117
A book about trains, huh?

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.450
Oh, that?

00:09:20.533 --> 00:09:22.075
Thought I'd learn something
about this railroad.

00:09:22.158 --> 00:09:24.283
Originally, it was
a short local line.

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:26.450
But it eventually grew and
became a way for the people

00:09:26.533 --> 00:09:28.700
in the area to get almost
anywhere in the country.

00:09:28.783 --> 00:09:29.992
Yeah?

00:09:30.075 --> 00:09:31.117
But what's interesting--

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.450
Is not this!

00:09:32.533 --> 00:09:34.700
There's nothing more lame
than a railroad geek!

00:09:34.783 --> 00:09:36.617
We should play
with these instead!

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:40.450
Whoa! You got an "Ahoy,
Steel Samurai!" That's cool.

00:09:40.533 --> 00:09:42.658
But, uh, what are we
gonna do with them?

00:09:42.742 --> 00:09:45.658
It's, like, so
obvious! C'mon, pal!

00:09:45.742 --> 00:09:46.908
We're gonna play bomb squad.

00:09:46.992 --> 00:09:49.367
Yeah! That's more like it!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:50.742
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:09:50.825 --> 00:09:53.117
High adventures with
runaway trains and bomb scares!

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.492
That sounds like fun to me!

00:09:54.575 --> 00:09:58.200
Wow, awesome!
You know how to play!

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:03.450
Right. It's
Sergeant Skip calling.

00:10:03.533 --> 00:10:06.867
Vangaurd, if you copy me,
come in, stat! Over!

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:07.950
[GUMSHOE]
I'm currently en route.

00:10:08.033 --> 00:10:09.492
Moving through car 2.

00:10:11.325 --> 00:10:14.075
And I'm entering
the third car, sergeant Skip!

00:10:14.158 --> 00:10:16.908
Now. Commence scanning
the perimeter for explosives!

00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:19.075
[MAYA]
Not so fast, ya moron!

00:10:19.158 --> 00:10:20.908
Don't you realize that
these passengers' lives

00:10:20.992 --> 00:10:22.200
are in our hands?

00:10:22.283 --> 00:10:25.408
So failure's not
an option! Ya dig?

00:10:25.492 --> 00:10:27.992
[GUMSHOE] Uh, yeah.
About the "moron" crack.

00:10:28.075 --> 00:10:29.658
Was that necessary?

00:10:29.742 --> 00:10:33.158
[MAYA] Don't sweat the
small stuff, Vanguard. Over.

00:10:33.242 --> 00:10:35.450
They are quite the pair.

00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:38.033
[GUMSHOE] Vanguard calling!
I've found the bomb!

00:10:38.117 --> 00:10:40.283
And it's a real doozy!

00:10:40.367 --> 00:10:42.533
[GUMSHOE] I've never seen
anything like it in my life!

00:10:42.617 --> 00:10:44.658
The thing has got
five freakin' wires!

00:10:44.742 --> 00:10:48.575
No way. Well.
Screw it, just cut 'em all!

00:10:48.658 --> 00:10:50.117
What?

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.367
But Sergeant Skip, the thing's
gonna explode if I do that!

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:53.408
[REGINA]
Excuse me, sir.

00:10:53.492 --> 00:10:54.533
[yelps]
Yeah?

00:10:54.617 --> 00:10:55.992
I mean, can I help
you with something?

00:10:56.075 --> 00:10:58.575
Is there a bomb?
I just overheard you.

00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:02.325
[laughs] No, sorry.
It's just a game.

00:11:02.408 --> 00:11:04.783
Ya know, luxury train.
Mysteries and whatnot?

00:11:04.867 --> 00:11:06.117
I see.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.283
Anyway, dinner service for
our car 3 passengers

00:11:09.367 --> 00:11:10.908
begins promptly at 6.

00:11:10.992 --> 00:11:13.158
[GUMSHOE]
Oh, okay. Sounds good to me!

00:11:13.242 --> 00:11:15.575
Ah, so the two cars have
dinner at different times.

00:11:15.658 --> 00:11:19.450
[GUMSHOE] Uh... Well,
I guess I'm gonna go dig in

00:11:19.533 --> 00:11:20.783
before it's gone.

00:11:26.242 --> 00:11:27.367
[gasps]

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.075
Hey.

00:11:29.158 --> 00:11:30.658
[GUMSHOE]
Really?

00:11:30.742 --> 00:11:32.783
You actually brought along the
ol' gavel with you on vacation?

00:11:32.867 --> 00:11:36.283
Yeah. Honestly, I just
don't feel complete without it.

00:11:36.367 --> 00:11:38.367
[laughs]

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:41.742
[BOTH chomp, sigh]

00:11:46.783 --> 00:11:48.408
[PHOENIX]
Almost 8 o'clock.

00:11:48.492 --> 00:11:50.783
Well, we should probably
get ready to go to dinner.

00:11:50.867 --> 00:11:52.075
Aye-aye!

00:12:12.617 --> 00:12:14.408
[BOTH slurp]

00:12:14.492 --> 00:12:15.700
Ah.

00:12:15.783 --> 00:12:17.575
One hell of a trip, ain't it?

00:12:17.658 --> 00:12:19.325
You said it, pal.

00:12:19.408 --> 00:12:20.492
[gasps]

00:12:20.575 --> 00:12:22.533
[GUMSHOE]
Hm? What's the matter, boss?

00:12:22.617 --> 00:12:24.492
Well, I'm afraid that
I must have forgotten something

00:12:24.575 --> 00:12:26.117
in the dining car.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.492
[MAYA]
Mm! Yummy!

00:12:28.575 --> 00:12:30.450
[gasps]
There's the judge.

00:12:32.825 --> 00:12:34.492
[MAYA]
Wonder what he's up to?

00:12:35.617 --> 00:12:38.325
[Good Morning to All plays]

00:12:38.408 --> 00:12:39.450
[JUDGE]
Hmm?

00:12:40.908 --> 00:12:43.033
[JAM]
Oh, dear, what's that?

00:12:43.117 --> 00:12:45.867
[gasps] They're putting
on some kind of show!

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.325
Jeez Louise.

00:12:49.408 --> 00:12:51.408
I didn't know there was
gonna be a blizzard comin'.

00:12:52.867 --> 00:12:55.575
Wait a second? What's going on?

00:12:58.867 --> 00:13:00.533
[gasps]

00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:06.200
Holy cow! Is that a human soul?

00:13:06.283 --> 00:13:08.908
--[brakes squealing]
--Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:13:10.617 --> 00:13:12.367
Why would they
stop the train out here?

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.450
Doesn't make a
lick o' sense to me.

00:13:14.533 --> 00:13:16.325
[crashing]

00:13:18.283 --> 00:13:20.158
What's up now?

00:13:30.575 --> 00:13:32.700
[whistle blows]

00:13:37.325 --> 00:13:38.617
[PHOENIX]
We're moving again.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.492
[sighs]
I wasn't expecting that.

00:13:41.575 --> 00:13:43.617
Excuse me.
Are you all right, ma'am?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.033
Yes, dearie.

00:13:45.117 --> 00:13:47.617
And aren't you just the
sweetest for asking about me.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.658
[gasps]
What was that all about?

00:13:50.742 --> 00:13:52.867
I swear that was
a person's soul out there.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:53.617
[REGINA]
Sir.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:54.908
[gasps, yelps]

00:13:58.033 --> 00:13:59.200
[gasps]

00:13:59.283 --> 00:14:00.992
Please be quiet!

00:14:01.075 --> 00:14:03.158
[GUMSHOE]
Hey, you're the guy!

00:14:03.242 --> 00:14:04.867
Who I am,
is the man taking control

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:06.075
over the Silver Star.

00:14:06.158 --> 00:14:07.700
You're doing what, now?

00:14:12.033 --> 00:14:13.617
I'll need your cell phone.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.408
We shall be confiscating
all communication devices.

00:14:16.492 --> 00:14:18.492
But if you do as we say,
you can rest assured,

00:14:18.575 --> 00:14:20.783
your safety is guaranteed.

00:14:20.867 --> 00:14:22.242
[PASSENGER A]
What's going on here?!

00:14:22.325 --> 00:14:23.533
[WOMAN screams]

00:14:23.617 --> 00:14:24.908
Please, sir, inside.

00:14:24.992 --> 00:14:26.200
[GUMSHOE growls]

00:14:27.658 --> 00:14:29.908
[GUMSHOE growls]
This is messed up.

00:14:31.117 --> 00:14:33.200
The judge went
back to the dining car.

00:14:33.283 --> 00:14:35.825
Phoenix and Maya, too.
I hope they're okay.

00:14:37.117 --> 00:14:39.033
[whistle blows]

00:14:45.742 --> 00:14:47.908
Hello, my name is Avery Richman.

00:14:47.992 --> 00:14:51.617
From the Goldstruck Republic.
Patriarch of the Richman Family.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.325
I'm also the owner
of the Silver Star Express.

00:14:54.408 --> 00:14:55.783
What's this about?

00:14:55.867 --> 00:14:57.825
[RICHMAN] First off,
I'd like to extend my deepest,

00:14:57.908 --> 00:15:00.575
heartfelt apologies
for scaring you like this.

00:15:00.658 --> 00:15:02.033
The purpose of the
guns in our hands

00:15:02.117 --> 00:15:04.283
is not to simply cause fear.

00:15:04.367 --> 00:15:06.658
They symbolize our
dedication to our cause.

00:15:06.742 --> 00:15:10.325
The resolve that we carry.
Please, try to understand that.

00:15:10.408 --> 00:15:11.825
And what's your cause?

00:15:11.908 --> 00:15:15.658
Heh. Let's take
things one step at a time.

00:15:15.742 --> 00:15:17.825
Now, if you would be so kind.

00:15:17.908 --> 00:15:20.075
Hand over any and all
communication devices

00:15:20.158 --> 00:15:21.450
you might have.

00:15:25.492 --> 00:15:26.492
[ATTENDANT B]
What is this?

00:15:26.575 --> 00:15:28.075
Ahoy, Steel Samurai.

00:15:28.158 --> 00:15:29.658
[ATTENDANT B]
Oh-kay?

00:15:29.742 --> 00:15:31.283
It's just a toy, really.

00:15:31.367 --> 00:15:32.700
[RICHMAN]
Let it go.

00:15:32.783 --> 00:15:36.658
I clearly told you not to
place anyone under duress.

00:15:36.742 --> 00:15:38.367
Please forgive me, sir.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.242
Apologies for his rudeness.

00:15:40.325 --> 00:15:41.825
Yeah. Sure.

00:15:41.908 --> 00:15:44.325
[JAM]
Avery Richman?

00:15:44.408 --> 00:15:46.617
[RICHMAN]
It's been quite a while, Madame.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:48.408
Uh. I'm sorry, sir.

00:15:48.492 --> 00:15:51.533
But weren't you sentenced to
death over in the United States?

00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:53.033
Really?

00:15:53.117 --> 00:15:56.700
Yes. One year ago,
I did stand trial for murder.

00:15:56.783 --> 00:15:58.617
And that travesty of
justice was held in

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.242
an American court of law.

00:16:00.325 --> 00:16:01.825
They declared me guilty.

00:16:01.908 --> 00:16:03.867
Then why are you in Japan now?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.867
I was in the process
of being transferred

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.325
to a Japanese prison.

00:16:07.408 --> 00:16:08.742
I see.

00:16:08.825 --> 00:16:11.283
Because you had become a
naturalized citizen of Japan.

00:16:11.367 --> 00:16:13.325
They decided to
extradite you back home.

00:16:13.408 --> 00:16:14.825
That's correct.

00:16:14.908 --> 00:16:17.908
I was ordered to return to
Japan to carry out my sentence.

00:16:17.992 --> 00:16:19.908
But I managed
to escape from the airport,

00:16:19.992 --> 00:16:22.908
and now I stand before
you aboard the Silver Star.

00:16:22.992 --> 00:16:25.450
Exactly how I had
been planning all along.

00:16:25.533 --> 00:16:27.700
So. It's part
of some larger plot?

00:16:27.783 --> 00:16:30.367
Yes. I have spent
innumerable hours

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.575
formulating my method of escape.

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:34.450
Of course, there's
no way I could've pulled off

00:16:34.533 --> 00:16:36.158
such an elaborate scheme alone.

00:16:36.242 --> 00:16:37.367
That's the reason I have

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.867
so many trustworthy
companions at my side.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.408
Every single one of them
is from my true homeland,

00:16:42.492 --> 00:16:44.408
the Goldstruck Republic.

00:16:44.492 --> 00:16:46.783
Their belief in my innocence
has remained steadfast

00:16:46.867 --> 00:16:48.450
throughout this ordeal.

00:16:48.533 --> 00:16:51.158
And they have supported
me every step of the way.

00:16:51.242 --> 00:16:53.492
My gratitude to them
knows no bounds.

00:16:53.575 --> 00:16:56.908
So to put it in other words,
they're all your accomplices.

00:16:56.992 --> 00:16:58.658
What's your end goal with this?

00:16:58.742 --> 00:17:01.700
You may be hidden inside your
own train for the time being.

00:17:01.783 --> 00:17:04.283
But it will reach its
destination tomorrow morning.

00:17:04.367 --> 00:17:05.700
And at that point...

00:17:05.783 --> 00:17:07.533
...it's game over.

00:17:07.617 --> 00:17:09.950
My goal, is but a simple one.

00:17:10.033 --> 00:17:11.408
I want a retrial.

00:17:11.492 --> 00:17:15.242
[whistle blows]

00:17:15.325 --> 00:17:18.200
Are you serious?
That's preposterous!

00:17:18.283 --> 00:17:20.492
The first trial
was a total sham.

00:17:20.575 --> 00:17:22.992
Nothing but false testimony
and faux evidence.

00:17:23.075 --> 00:17:25.033
Lies upon more lies!

00:17:25.117 --> 00:17:28.825
And I'll present my case before
you tonight to prove it!

00:17:28.908 --> 00:17:31.325
Is that so? How exactly?

00:17:31.408 --> 00:17:34.325
It's beginning
right here and right now!

00:17:34.408 --> 00:17:35.783
On this train.

00:17:35.867 --> 00:17:39.992
With all of you present.
I have my retrial!

00:17:40.075 --> 00:17:43.450
[gasping]

00:17:43.533 --> 00:17:45.200
[PHOENIX]
But Mr. Richman,

00:17:45.283 --> 00:17:47.325
you realize you're
on a running train.

00:17:47.408 --> 00:17:49.658
How you do plan on
doing that here?

00:17:49.742 --> 00:17:53.325
[RICHMAN] This rail car has
everything we need for a trial.

00:17:53.408 --> 00:17:56.325
There's a courtroom...
and witnesses!

00:18:06.492 --> 00:18:08.033
That is the reason.

00:18:08.117 --> 00:18:10.867
I specifically
invited each of you.

00:18:14.617 --> 00:18:17.450
Seems we've got ourselves into
one hell of a pickle here.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.325
[REGINA clears throat]

00:18:25.408 --> 00:18:26.700
I'm gonna ask you nicely.

00:18:26.783 --> 00:18:28.367
Please, get back inside.

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:29.825
[GUMSHOE growls]

00:18:29.908 --> 00:18:31.658
I'm afraid I don't
understand exactly how

00:18:31.742 --> 00:18:34.283
we here could
qualify as witnesses.

00:18:34.367 --> 00:18:37.492
[RICHMAN] Everyone I invited
to travel in car 1

00:18:37.575 --> 00:18:40.325
is related to my case
in some form or fashion.

00:18:40.408 --> 00:18:42.242
Nobody can deny
their involvement.

00:18:42.325 --> 00:18:44.242
[gasping]

00:18:44.325 --> 00:18:46.325
Yeah? So who'll defend you?

00:18:46.408 --> 00:18:48.408
I'm surprised you must ask.

00:18:48.492 --> 00:18:52.033
It'll be you, of course,
Mr. Phoenix Wright!

00:18:52.117 --> 00:18:53.825
You've shown outstanding skill.

00:18:53.908 --> 00:18:56.283
Why else would I have invited
you aboard my train?

00:18:56.367 --> 00:18:58.325
[MAYA]
What about a prosecutor?

00:18:58.408 --> 00:19:01.200
Am I correct to
assume that would be me?

00:19:01.283 --> 00:19:03.700
[RICHMAN]
Exactly, Mister Turnbull.

00:19:03.783 --> 00:19:05.575
[PHOENIX]
Who's that?

00:19:05.658 --> 00:19:08.033
I'm with the United States
Attorney's Office.

00:19:08.117 --> 00:19:09.867
Tristan Turnbull, esquire.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.033
[rattling]

00:19:11.117 --> 00:19:12.783
Who's there?!

00:19:12.867 --> 00:19:15.450
[JUDGE]
M-Me...?

00:19:15.533 --> 00:19:16.908
Why's the judge in here?

00:19:16.992 --> 00:19:18.742
We did see him come in earlier.

00:19:18.825 --> 00:19:20.408
You're a judge are you?

00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:22.617
[JUDGE] I just came back
to collect my gavel.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.533
But if I'd known about all this,

00:19:24.617 --> 00:19:27.992
I would have certainly stayed
inside my traveling compartment.

00:19:28.075 --> 00:19:29.783
What a coincidence this is.

00:19:29.867 --> 00:19:32.242
How lucky we are to have
a sitting judge among us

00:19:32.325 --> 00:19:33.700
to preside over the trial.

00:19:33.783 --> 00:19:35.742
So will you do
the honors, Your Honor?

00:19:35.825 --> 00:19:37.158
Well, I suppose I can.

00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:39.242
If you insist. That is.

00:19:39.325 --> 00:19:40.700
What is forcibly
holding a trial on

00:19:40.783 --> 00:19:42.200
a train supposed to do?

00:19:42.283 --> 00:19:44.200
We're completely isolated here.

00:19:44.283 --> 00:19:46.325
[RICHMAN] I have set up
cameras and transceivers

00:19:46.408 --> 00:19:47.950
to broadcast the trial.

00:19:48.033 --> 00:19:49.908
In the end... they will see.

00:19:49.992 --> 00:19:52.075
I will brandish the truth
in the faces of those

00:19:52.158 --> 00:19:53.283
who have wronged me!

00:19:53.367 --> 00:19:54.658
In the end?

00:19:54.742 --> 00:19:56.825
The Silver Star
arrives at her destination

00:19:56.908 --> 00:19:59.117
at 7 AM. At the same time,

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.408
we'll be seeing the first
sunrise of the year.

00:20:01.492 --> 00:20:04.117
My wish is for the truth
to be uncovered by then.

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.700
I have a question for you.

00:20:05.783 --> 00:20:07.658
What do you plan to do
if this trial finds that

00:20:07.742 --> 00:20:10.450
you're guilty as well?

00:20:10.533 --> 00:20:12.533
I will accept
the verdict reached.

00:20:12.617 --> 00:20:15.283
However, I'm quite sure
that won't happen.

00:20:15.367 --> 00:20:18.325
Not as long as the trial is
conducted properly and fairly.

00:20:18.408 --> 00:20:19.617
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:21.450
[TRISTAN] Hmph. Mr. Richman,
our justice system

00:20:21.533 --> 00:20:23.533
does not make mistakes.

00:20:23.617 --> 00:20:25.158
I understand.

00:20:25.242 --> 00:20:28.325
And I agree to act
as your defense.

00:20:28.408 --> 00:20:31.617
[RICHMAN] You have my humble
thanks, Mr. Wright!

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:34.325
[TRISTAN] Give me 20 minutes.
I'll need to prepare.

00:20:36.908 --> 00:20:39.783
Um. Hey. Excuse me, mister.

00:20:39.867 --> 00:20:41.867
I think I ate a little too much.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.575
Permission to go
to the bathroom?

00:20:43.658 --> 00:20:44.575
[RICHMAN]
Go ahead.

00:20:44.658 --> 00:20:46.033
Thank you, sir!

00:20:49.992 --> 00:20:51.450
[MAYA]
Come in, Gumshoe.

00:20:51.533 --> 00:20:52.783
[yelps]

00:20:52.867 --> 00:20:55.075
[MAYA]
Gumshoe, please respond!

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.283
Gumshoe speaking.

00:20:58.367 --> 00:21:00.325
What in the hell's
going on up there?

00:21:01.742 --> 00:21:04.492
[MAYA]
Yeah. So that's the whole story.

00:21:04.575 --> 00:21:07.158
Detective. Nick really
needs your help right now!

00:21:07.242 --> 00:21:08.492
I read you.

00:21:08.575 --> 00:21:11.075
I'm still back in my room
in car 3 at the moment,

00:21:11.158 --> 00:21:13.158
but the dining car
is the next one over.

00:21:13.242 --> 00:21:14.950
I'll try to make my way there.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:22.283
[REGINA gasps]
Hold it!

00:21:22.825 --> 00:21:24.283
--[yelps]
--[gun firing]

00:21:24.367 --> 00:21:26.783
[GUMSHOE groans]

00:21:26.867 --> 00:21:28.200
Are you serious, lady?

00:21:28.283 --> 00:21:29.825
[GUMSHOE groans]

00:21:33.533 --> 00:21:35.783
What the... Wait. No way!

00:21:35.867 --> 00:21:38.450
What in the hell is happening?

00:21:38.533 --> 00:21:40.117
Where's the dining car?!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.950
It's supposed to be right here!

00:21:42.033 --> 00:21:45.075
And it looks
like car 1 is gone, too!

00:23:20.033 --> 00:23:21.408
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:21.492 --> 00:23:23.908
Could the international
fugitive Avery Richman

00:23:23.992 --> 00:23:25.283
really be innocent?

00:23:25.367 --> 00:23:28.033
My opponent, American
prosecutor Tristan Turnbull,

00:23:28.117 --> 00:23:29.658
presents scores of evidence.

00:23:29.742 --> 00:23:32.908
All of it reinforces Richman's
earlier guilty verdict.

00:23:32.992 --> 00:23:35.325
To make matters worse,
one of the key witnesses

00:23:35.408 --> 00:23:38.075
is found murdered
on board the speeding train.

00:23:38.158 --> 00:23:39.992
Who could the killer be?

00:23:40.075 --> 00:23:42.700
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:42.783 --> 00:23:46.158
Next episode, "Northward,
Turnabout Express -- 2nd Trial"!

00:23:46.242 --> 00:23:47.575
Take that!
